   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The relative pronoun in the accusative",
     "texto": [
      "In the accusative only the masculine changes: **den** (which, that). The feminine, the neuter and the plural don't change: **die**, **das**, **die**. Example: **Der Koffer, den ich habe, ist schwer** (the suitcase I have is heavy).",
      "Feminine example: **Die Stadt, die ich besuche** (the city I visit). Neuter: **Das Hotel, das ich buche** (the hotel I book)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Be careful with den and dem",
     "texto": [
      "**den** is the masculine accusative relative pronoun. **dem** is dative and doesn't work here; you'll see it later.",
      "With the Perfekt, the auxiliary goes at the end of the relative clause: **Das Ticket, das ich gekauft habe** (the ticket I bought)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
